# The lanes of the host's pair rows against the scalar row on a dense
# system, at the bound of the order of a sum (D402;
# Inputs/host_pair_lanes_bound.py says how the bound is made). The dipeptide
# in water with PME: ten types, the exclusions of its topology, rows of the
# list of 118 to 371 candidates, 1,017 of 1,168 not a multiple of 8, so that
# the padding of a tail repeats a candidate. The loops over pairs take
# host(lanes(W)), checked from the remarks of the chooser. lanes(8) and
# lanes(4) at step 0 in double and mixed precision: every force component
# and the potential within the bound, from the terms of the rows alone. A
# tail whose padding is not masked gives ratios of 1e10; a skipped, a
# doubled, or a misgathered candidate is a term outside the order of the
# sum, which the bound leaves out. The order of the lanes' combination is
# pinned by host-pair-lanes-w8.mlir, not here: any order of the same terms
# is within the bound.
#
# REQUIRES: python-api, parmed
#
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/host_pair_lanes_bound.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide mdir-opt Double 8 4 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=DOUBLE
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/host_pair_lanes_bound.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide mdir-opt Mixed 8 4 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=MIXED

# DOUBLE: rows of the list (within the reach): 118 to 371 candidates; 1017 of 1168 not a multiple of 8
# DOUBLE: lanes(8): 3 loops over pairs take host(lanes(8)), none keeps the scalar row
# DOUBLE: Double lanes(8): {{.*}}: within the bound
# DOUBLE: lanes(4): 3 loops over pairs take host(lanes(4)), none keeps the scalar row
# DOUBLE: Double lanes(4): {{.*}}: within the bound
# DOUBLE: all within the bound
# MIXED: lanes(8): 3 loops over pairs take host(lanes(8)), none keeps the scalar row
# MIXED: Mixed lanes(8): {{.*}}: within the bound
# MIXED: lanes(4): 3 loops over pairs take host(lanes(4)), none keeps the scalar row
# MIXED: Mixed lanes(4): {{.*}}: within the bound
# MIXED: all within the bound
